cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BioModelling Pro: biogeography and species distribution modelling in the browser"
abstract: >-
  BioModelling Pro is a self-contained web application for biogeographic analysis and species
  distribution modelling that runs entirely in the browser, with no installation and no
  server-side computation. It downloads presence records from GBIF, filters and cleans them
  with nine coordinate-quality rules, extracts bioclimatic, elevation, Koeppen-Geiger climate
  and soil variables, and explores them with descriptive statistics, normality tests,
  correlation and collinearity diagnostics, principal component analysis, clustering,
  correspondence analysis and ecological metrics of range, spatial pattern and niche. It fits
  ten species distribution algorithms (a MaxEnt-style penalised logistic model, GLM, GAM,
  random forest, boosted regression trees, support vector machine, neural network, Bioclim,
  Domain and Mahalanobis distance) and an ensemble, validates them with spatial blocks, AUC,
  TSS and the Boyce index, and projects them to climate scenarios with extrapolation maps.
  The interface is bilingual (Spanish and English) with light and dark themes.
